INT. COUNTY COURTHOUSE - LOADING DOCK - DAY

Concrete. Rolling carts. Evidence boxes stacked to the ceiling. A freight elevator groans.

ATTORNEY NADIA BRENNAN, 30s, sharp suit, sneakers, drags a box off a cart. ATTORNEY ELI MORROW, 50s, rumpled, waits with a clipboard. Opposing counsel. Neither smiles.

ELI
You're late.

NADIA
Your clerk lost the key.

ELI
She never loses keys.

NADIA
She lost this one.

She pops the lid. Inside: a ledger, water-stained. Eli goes still.

ELI
That's not on the inventory.

NADIA
It is now.

JUDGE OKONKWO-REYES, 60s, robe over a windbreaker, appears at the elevator door. Cigarette unlit between her fingers. Nadia and Eli straighten.

JUDGE OKONKWO-REYES
Counselors. Tell me why a sealed ledger is sitting on a dock.

ELI
Your Honor, she tampered with a chain of custody.

NADIA
He moved it. I found it.

JUDGE OKONKWO-REYES
She found it. He moved it. Wonderful.

Eli lunges for the ledger. Nadia jerks it away. Boxes topple. A bailiff, DEPUTY HALE, 20s, bursts in from the stairwell, hand on holster.

DEPUTY HALE
Freeze! Everybody!

All three freeze. Eli with one hand out. Nadia clutching the ledger. The Judge, calm, lights her cigarette.

JUDGE OKONKWO-REYES
Deputy. Stand down. They're lawyers. They only bite on the record.

Hale lowers his hand. Exhales.

JUDGE OKONKWO-REYES (CONT'D)
Give me the ledger. Both of you. My chambers, ten minutes.

Nadia hands it over. Eli sags against a cart.

ELI
She'll bury us.

NADIA
Not her. She's deciding who gets to dig.

The elevator doors close on the Judge. Deputy Hale picks up a fallen box. Sets it carefully back on the stack.
